# Scalar Multiplication

Multiply each element of the matrix by $-\frac{1}{4}$:

$$-\frac{1}{4}\left(
\begin{array}{ccc}
 9 & 7 & 2 \\
 7 & -8 & -1 \\
\end{array}
\right) = \left(
\begin{array}{ccc}
 -\frac{1}{4}(9) & -\frac{1}{4}(7) & -\frac{1}{4}(2) \\
 -\frac{1}{4}(7) & -\frac{1}{4}(-8) & -\frac{1}{4}(-1) \\
\end{array}
\right)$$

**Result:**

$$\left(
\begin{array}{ccc}
 -\dfrac{9}{4} & -\dfrac{7}{4} & -\dfrac{1}{2} \\
 -\dfrac{7}{4} & 2 & \dfrac{1}{4} \\
\end{array}
\right)$$

